@equalang/dsh-plugin README · Costs and privacy：- Jobs spend your Equalang credits, the same balance as on the website. `estimate_cost` is free. DeepSeek Harness runs MCP tools without asking you first, so the agreement comes from the model: the server tells it to say the cost and get your agreement before a job. Credits are bought at <https://equalang.com/pricing>. The model the agent runs on is billed separately, by DeepSeek or whichever provider you chose.
- A file you ask to translate is uploaded to Equalang to be processed. See the [privacy policy](https://equalang.com/legal/privacy).
- Like every MCP server DeepSeek Harness starts, this one runs outside the agent's sandbox: it reads the file you name and writes its results beside it under any permission preset.

@equalang/dsh-plugin README · Troubleshooting：- **No Equalang tools.** Check that the plugin is enabled under **Plugins**, and restart after installing from a terminal. DeepSeek Harness refuses to install or start a plugin made for another version of itself, and says which version it needs.
- **`EQUALANG_API_KEY is not set`.** Save the key in one of the places above. An `export` in your shell alone does not reach the server.
- **Installed from a terminal, missing in the desktop app.** `dsh plugin --profile web` installs into the `web` profile; the desktop app uses its own. Install through the app's **Plugins** page.

@equalang/dsh-plugin README · Also from Equalang：- [equalang-mcp](https://github.com/equalang/equalang-mcp), the MCP server this plugin runs, for Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and other MCP clients.
- [equalang-skill](https://github.com/equalang/equalang-skill), the same operations as an Agent Skill. DeepSeek Harness also loads skills from `~/.agents/skills`.
- The Equalang API: <https://equalang.com/llms.txt>
